<title>PHILIPPINES: Reynolds eyes petrochemical projects.</title>
<headline>Reynolds eyes petrochemical projects.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aluminium producer Reynolds Philippines Corp said on Wednesday it planned to diversify and invest in petrochemical projects.</p>
<p>Reynolds told the Philippine Stock Exchange (PSE) that it was negotiating with BP Holdings International B.V. of the British Petroleum group, Sumitomo Corp and the Malaysian national oil firm Petroliam Nasional Berhad (Petronas) for several petrochemical ventures.</p>
<p>Reynolds president Jimmy Gonzalez told Reuters that Reynolds was invited by British Petroleum.</p>
<p>&quot;Everything is still premature. We can't divulge yet the stake or what type of petrochemical project we will invest in,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said details of Reynold's petrochemical venture will be presented to the stockholders on June 30 for their approval.</p>
<p>Reynolds will also seek authority to borrow long-term loans for the firm's operational requirements, its advisory said.</p>
